MERGE (n:R2G:`Symbol` {id: "sym:scripts/bench_real_repos.py::covered_lines_r2g"}) SET n += {`id`: "sym:scripts/bench_real_repos.py::covered_lines_r2g", `name`: "covered_lines_r2g", `qualname`: "covered_lines_r2g", `kind`: "function", `path`: "scripts/bench_real_repos.py", `lang`: "python", `start_line`: 153, `end_line`: 181, `signature`: "def covered_lines_r2g(pack: dict, root: Path) -> dict[str, set[int]]:", `docstring`: "Source lines whose text is actually in the pack, per path.\n\n    A chunk's `start_line`/`end_line` describe the whole symbol, not the text\n    returned: a split symbol's later parts, a file residual with its symbols cut\n    out, and a neighbour compressed to its signature all return less than that\n    range. So each returned line is aligned, in order, to the next source line\n    in the symbol's range with the same text. Synthetic header lines\n    (`# file:`, `# calls:`, ...) match nothing and earn nothing."};
